<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="62e2efda">&lt;p&gt;
    A solution requirement captures the overall characteristics of a business solution. It typically contains higher-level
    descriptions of the business capability needed. Solution requirements are eventually decomposed into business
    requirements and system requirement types (functional and non-functional).
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Example: “The solution must integrate our sales process across our physical and digital retail channels.”
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="f3283b"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="6060db6e"></attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="7e3f7233"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="c79aeb70">&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        To formally describe what is required by the business solution.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        To be a starting point for requirements before being analyzed and decomposed into business requirements and system
        requirement types (functional and non-functional).
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
